WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.925
Use Upgrade Advisor to identify evidence needed before an upgrade Enter the

00:00:04.925 --> 00:00:09.920
cluster context and reviewed P E and optional P C connections

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:15.412
Establish verified certificate trust first The advisor does not execute

00:00:15.412 --> 00:00:20.662
upgrades or certify a supported upgrade path Verify T L

00:00:20.662 --> 00:00:26.008
S certificate is enabled separately for P E and P C inventory collection

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:30.388
Administrators can use an explicitly scoped temporary exception where

00:00:30.388 --> 00:00:35.250
authorized It resets after collection is audited and is

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:39.482
preserved as a qualification in saved inventory and assessment reports

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:44.350
Review that qualification with the findings An exception weakens identity

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:48.400
assurance for that collection it is not a trust repair or a general workflow

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:53.675
setting Other workflows drift checks and recovery keep their own certificate

00:00:53.675 --> 00:00:54.520
policies

00:00:54.866 --> 00:00:59.354
Collect fresh inventory and inspect the timestamp, returned fields

00:00:59.466 --> 00:01:00.504
and collection errors.

00:01:00.904 --> 00:01:05.004
P E cluster and host reads can supply A O S and

00:01:05.004 --> 00:01:07.741
homogeneous A H V versions.

00:01:08.154 --> 00:01:12.904
P C product-header detection is limited context, not an authenticated

00:01:12.904 --> 00:01:13.779
permission test.

00:01:14.166 --> 00:01:16.854
Other components can remain manual or unknown.

00:01:17.266 --> 00:01:19.791
Do not replace missing values with guessed versions.

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:24.512
Enter the intended target versions and environment signals.

00:01:24.912 --> 00:01:30.200
Review release notes, compatibility, lifecycle prechecks and any dark-site

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:32.887
bundle requirements using the actual vendor material.

00:01:33.287 --> 00:01:36.237
Mark evidence complete only when it was reviewed.

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:41.300
Curated rule packs contribute explicit guardrails and sources.

00:01:41.712 --> 00:01:45.762
They are not an automatic scrape of every support article or private

00:01:45.762 --> 00:01:46.612
defect record.

00:01:47.808 --> 00:01:52.945
Run the assessment and review each blocker, warning, review item and

00:01:52.958 --> 00:01:53.433
unknown.

00:01:53.833 --> 00:01:57.833
Read the guidance, source and missing evidence rather than looking

00:01:57.908 --> 00:01:59.358
only at an overall score.

00:01:59.758 --> 00:02:03.208
Assign the necessary follow-up and collect its real evidence.

00:02:03.608 --> 00:02:07.721
A clear result remains limited to the reviewed inputs and rules;

00:02:08.121 --> 00:02:12.445
it does not replace actual lifecycle checks or authorize change execution.

00:02:13.629 --> 00:02:17.979
Save the reviewed assessment with its owner and context, then export

00:02:17.979 --> 00:02:19.991
the evidence bundle if required.

00:02:20.391 --> 00:02:23.841
The snapshot preserves the assessed inputs and findings.

00:02:24.229 --> 00:02:28.716
Collecting newer inventory later does not rewrite that saved assessment.

00:02:29.116 --> 00:02:33.241
Compare a new snapshot when conditions change and retain the relevant

00:02:33.241 --> 00:02:36.941
version with the change record and final vendor precheck results.
